        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Suppose that we wish to solve the compound inequality </p>",
            "readable_text": "Suppose that we wish to solve the compound inequality",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4 \\le x + 2 \\le 8.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: 4 \\le x + 2 \\le 8.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To solve the compound inequality, we apply the usual operations to the middle of the inequality to isolate <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x.]</span> Keep in mind that whatever we do to the middle, we also need to do to <em>both</em> the left-hand <em>and</em> right-hand sides.</p>",
            "readable_text": "To solve the compound inequality, we apply the usual operations to the middle of the inequality to isolate [MATH: x.] Keep in mind that whatever we do to the middle, we also need to do to both the left-hand and right-hand sides.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Here, we can isolate <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x]</span> by subtracting <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2\\mathbin{:}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Here, we can isolate [MATH: x] by subtracting [MATH: 2\\mathbin{:}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\eqalign{\n4 &amp; \\le x + 2 \\le 8 \\[5pt]\n4 \\,{\\color{red}-}\\, {\\color{red}{2}} &amp;\\le x + 2 \\,{\\color{red}-}\\, {\\color{red}{2}} \\le 8 \\,{\\color{red}-}\\, {\\color{red}{2}} \\[5pt]\n2 &amp;\\le x \\le 6\n}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \\eqalign{\n4 & \\le x + 2 \\le 8 \\[5pt]\n4 \\,{\\color{red}-}\\, {\\color{red}{2}} &\\le x + 2 \\,{\\color{red}-}\\, {\\color{red}{2}} \\le 8 \\,{\\color{red}-}\\, {\\color{red}{2}} \\[5pt]\n2 &\\le x \\le 6\n}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Therefore, the solution is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2 \\le x \\le 6.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Therefore, the solution is [MATH: 2 \\le x \\le 6.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nSuppose that we wish to solve the compound inequality\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 4 \\le x + 2 \\le 8.]\n\nContent:\nTo solve the compound inequality, we apply the usual operations to the middle of the inequality to isolate [MATH: x.] Keep in mind that whatever we do to the middle, we also need to do to both the left-hand and right-hand sides.\n\nContent:\nHere, we can isolate [MATH: x] by subtracting [MATH: 2\\mathbin{:}]\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n4 & \\le x + 2 \\le 8 \\[5pt]\n4 \\,{\\color{red}-}\\, {\\color{red}{2}} &\\le x + 2 \\,{\\color{red}-}\\, {\\color{red}{2}} \\le 8 \\,{\\color{red}-}\\, {\\color{red}{2}} \\[5pt]\n2 &\\le x \\le 6\n}]\n\nContent:\nTherefore, the solution is [MATH: 2 \\le x \\le 6.]"
      },
